---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// Privacy Policy Page
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | December"
  description="Privacy Policy for December CLI and Cloud."
  canonicalUrl="https://trydecember.com/privacy"
  activePath="/privacy"
  hideHeader={false}
  hideFooter={false}
>
  <!-- Main Container: Identical horizontal gap/margins to landing page and docs page -->
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[940px] px-6 sm:px-8 md:px-10 lg:px-12 pt-8 pb-16 sm:pt-12 sm:pb-24 min-w-0">
    <!-- Breadcrumb Navigation Bar -->
    <nav class="flex items-center flex-wrap font-mono text-xs text-[#64748b] mb-8">
      <div class="flex items-center flex-wrap gap-2">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-[#090a0f] transition-colors">home</a>
        <span class="text-[#cbd5e1]">/</span>
        <span class="text-[#64748b]">legal</span>
        <span class="text-[#cbd5e1]">/</span>
        <span class="text-[#090a0f] font-medium">[privacy]</span>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <!-- Article Layout: Spans full width matching landing page & docs structure -->
    <article class="w-full min-w-0">
      <!-- Document Header -->
      <header class="mb-8 max-w-3xl min-w-0">
        <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-medium tracking-tight text-[#090a0f] leading-snug">
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-2.5 text-sm sm:text-[15px] text-[#52525b] leading-relaxed">
          December is built for developers. We believe your code, prompts, and credentials belong strictly to you. This policy explains what data we collect, how it is used, and how it is protected.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Markdown / Body Content -->
      <div class="docs-prose min-w-0 max-w-full text-[#52525b] text-sm sm:text-[15px] leading-relaxed">
        <section>
          <h2>How December Handles Your Code</h2>
          <p>
            December operates in two modes:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Local Mode (CLI):</strong> December runs directly on your computer. Your files, folders, git history, and environment variables stay on your machine. Nothing is uploaded to December servers.</li>
            <li><strong>Cloud Mode:</strong> When you use cloud workspaces, your project runs inside an isolated, private sandbox. Only files needed for your active task are transferred over an encrypted connection.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
          <p>We only collect the minimum information required to run the service:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Account details:</strong> Your name, email, and account ID when you sign in with GitHub or Google.</li>
            <li><strong>API keys (BYOK):</strong> If you bring your own API keys, they are encrypted and used solely to route prompts to your chosen AI provider.</li>
            <li><strong>Session history:</strong> Prompts, tool execution steps, and diffs so you can review your history in the web dashboard.</li>
            <li><strong>Anonymous telemetry:</strong> Basic CLI speed and crash diagnostics. We never capture code, file contents, passwords, or personal paths. You can turn telemetry off anytime in settings.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>We Do Not Train On Your Code</h2>
          <p>
            We do not use your source code, prompts, git repositories, or Google account information to train or fine-tune artificial intelligence models.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Google Sign-In & Limited Use</h2>
          <p>
            December's use of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
            <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#87b2f4] hover:underline">
              Google API Services User Data Policy
            </a>, including the Limited Use requirements.
          </p>
          <p>
            When you sign in with Google, we only access your basic profile (full name, email address, profile picture, and Google ID) to log you in and send essential account updates. We never sell your Google data, share it with advertisers or data brokers, or use it for marketing.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Your API Keys Are Private</h2>
          <p>
            Your AI provider keys (Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, DeepSeek) are stored encrypted. They are never shared between accounts, never logged in readable text, and never accessible to staff.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Private Cloud Sandboxes</h2>
          <p>
            Cloud tasks run inside dedicated Linux containers. Sandboxes are never shared between users. When your task ends or times out, the sandbox is completely wiped.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Third-Party AI Models</h2>
          <p>
            When you ask December to write code, it sends your prompt and relevant file context directly to the model provider you chose (such as Anthropic, OpenAI, or Google). Under our agreements with these providers, your requests are not used to train their models.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Deleting Your Data</h2>
          <p>You can delete your data at any time:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Delete individual chat sessions from the web dashboard.</li>
            <li>Deleting your account permanently wipes all your stored keys, sessions, and billing history.</li>
            <li>Old temporary cloud logs are automatically deleted after 30 days.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Security & Questions</h2>
          <p>
            All network communication is encrypted with TLS. If you have any privacy questions or security concerns, email us directly at
            <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:team@trydecember.com">team@trydecember.com</a><!--/email_off-->.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <!-- Navigation & Contact -->
      <div class="mt-14 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4 font-mono text-xs">
        <span class="text-[#64748b]">
          Questions? <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:team@trydecember.com" class="text-[#87b2f4] hover:underline">team@trydecember.com</a><!--/email_off-->
        </span>
        <a
          href="/terms"
          class="group inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 p-2.5 border border-[#e2e8f0] bg-white hover:border-[#87b2f4] text-[#090a0f] transition-all"
        >
          <span>Terms of Service</span>
          <span class="text-[#94a3b8] group-hover:text-[#87b2f4] transition-colors">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
